The half-life of a software engineering skill is now approximately 2.5 years; even core programming languages are replaced by new ones within a decade — continuous learning is not optional in tech.
Countries with the highest investment in adult education (Sweden, Netherlands, Denmark) have the highest adaptability to economic shocks and the lowest long-term unemployment rates.
IBM's 'new collar' job initiative trains workers for cloud, AI, and cybersecurity roles in 12–18 months — demonstrating that adults can acquire highly valued skills rapidly when given access.
